>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>I am Hegesipos, (son) of Bulis\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca class=\"translation-source\" href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/LHNEVHEN\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/LHNEVHEN\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Hegesippos sono, (figlio) di Bulis\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>A number of other uninscribed stele have been found in the necropolis, but this is the only funerary inscription from ancient Mylai to date, and parallels in the Euboean alphabet in the region are rare.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Ollà Ravesi Sardella Zavettieri 2025 48 fig.40 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Boffa 2025 608-621, figs. 1-2. \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>The script employs the Euboean alphabet\u003C/p> Line 1-2  40-75  Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[180,183,186,189,192,194,197,200,203],{"id":181,"html":182},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/LHNEVHEN\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/LHNEVHEN\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>Ͱε̄γέ̄σιπός ἐ̄μ \u003Cspan class=\"tei text-direction